From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 host credential leak events (ABI 1.60)

Security audit RC-500 F-09, engine part. Bridge 0.63.0, feature
credential_leak_events.
ChromePasswordManagerClient::NotifyUserCredentialsWereLeaked handed a found
leak to the ManagePasswordsUIController registry tabs lack, so it was dropped
while Settings promised a warning. In a registry tab it now posts
ReArcCredentialLeakEvent (tab identity, CredentialLeakFlags, origin, username;
never the password) to ReArcEngineSetCredentialLeakCallback. No callback:
dropped, as before.

Last rebased: 2026-11-10 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.96 (2ad9b7f5a8).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

